--1.Project Overview
The Student Performance Analysis System is a Python-based project used to analyze student marks and academic
performance.It reads student information from an input csv file & calculate total and average marks,grades
identifies pass or fail,rank of students & Finally generates performance reports.

The project uses Python libraries such as Pandas and NumPy to process and analyze student data.Finally,it saves
the processed information into a new CSV file...


--2.Problem Statement
Calculating student totals,averages marks,grades,ranks,and overall performance manually.It is time-consuming and
may lead to errors.An automated system is required to perform these calculations accurately and display the
results in an organized format.

This project solves the problem by using Python to analyze student marks automatically and generate useful
performance reports...


--3.Objectives
The main objectives of the project are:
*To read student details and marks from an input file.
*To calculate the total and average marks of each student.
*To assign grades based on average marks.
*To identify whether each student has passed or failed.
*To rank students according to their total marks.
*To calculate overall student performance.
*To analyze subject-wise performance...


--4.Technologies Used
Python:Python is the main programming language used to implement the project.It performs calculations,applies
conditions and generates reports.

Pandas:Pandas is used to read student data,organize it into a DataFrame,calculate totals and averages,assign ranks
analyze performance,and export the results.

NumPy:NumPy is imported for numerical operations.

CSV File:CSV files are used to store Data...


--5.Input Data
The program uses student information containing the following fields:
*Student_ID–Unique identification number of each student.
*Name–Name of the student.
*Department–Department or branch of the student.
*Html,CSS,JavaScript,Java,Python Subhects-Marks Obtained in the Subjects
*Attendance–Total No.of Classess Attended.
The subject columns are used to calculate total and average marks...


--6.Implementation of the Project
*Import Libraries:Import Pandas and NumPy for data processing and numerical operations.
*Read Student Data:Load student records from the input file into a Pandas DataFrame.
*Define Subjects:Create a list containing All Subjects.
*Display Student Data:Print the original students csv file in a tabular format.
*Calculate Total Marks:Add the marks of all five subjects for each student.
*Calculate Average Marks:Calculate the average marks obtained by each student.
*Assign Grades:Assign grades based on students average Marks using conditional statements(if,elif,else).
*Determine Pass/Fail:Mark students as Pass if their average is at least 40,otherwise mark them as Fail.
*Rank Students:Rank students in descending order according to their total scores and assign ranks.
*Analyze Overall Performance:Calculate the total,passed,and failed students,along with highest,lowest and average
performance of All Students.
*Analyze Subject-Wise Performance:Calculate the highest,lowest and average marks for each subject.
*Identify Top Performers:Select the top three students based on their total Marks.
*Export Results:Save the processed student records and calculated results into another csv file...


--7.Expected Output
When the program executes successfully, it displays the following sections in the terminal:
*STUDENTS DATA:Displays the original student records.
*TOTAL Marks:Displays the total marks of each student.
*AVERAGE Marks:Displays the average marks of each student.
*GRADES:Displays the grades assigned to students.
*PASS/FAIL:Displays the pass or fail status of students.
*RANKED STUDENTS:Displays students in rank order.
*PERFORMANCE:Displays overall class performance statistics.
*SUBJECT WISE PERFORMANCE:Displays the highest,lowest,average marks for each subject.
*TOP PERFORMERS:Displays up to three students with the highest total marks...


--8.Output File
The program generates a file named Students_Output.csv.
This file contains the original student details along with the calculated total & average marks,grades,pass/fail
status and rank.

The output file can be opened using Microsoft Excel,text editor...


--9.Advantages
*Reduces manual calculations.
*Saves time when processing multiple student records.
*Provides consistent calculations for all students.
*Makes student ranking easier.
*Identifies the highest and lowest scores.
*Provides subject-wise performance statistics.
*Identifies top-performing students.
*Stores the processed results for future reference...


--10.Limitations
*The program requires a correctly formatted input file.
*Missing or non-numeric marks may affect calculations.
*The grade criteria may need to be modified according to institutional rules.
*Pass/fail status is determined only by the overall average.
*Attendance is recorded but is not considered in the analysis.
*The program displays text-based reports rather than graphical charts...


--11.Future Scope
The project can be improved by adding a graphical user interface to make it easier to use.Charts and graphs can
be included to represent student and subject performance visually.Data validation can be added to handle missing
marks and incorrect values.

The system could also be extended to generate individual student report cards,export PDF reports,analyze
attendance and store records in a database...


--12.Conclusion
The Student Performance Analysis System successfully demonstrates how Python can be used to automate
student-result analysis.By using Pandas,the project calculates total and average marks,assigns grades,determines
pass/fail status,rank of students,analyzes subject-wise performance and identifies top performers.

The system reduces manual work,organizes student information and generates useful reports for understanding
academic performance.The final results are saved in a CSV file,making them easy to access and reuse.

Overall, this project provides a simple and useful application of Python programming and data analysis techniques
in the education field.